# SQLite databases generated by running the Forecast Models / Humanizer
# Python pipelines locally — database.sql is the source of truth, these
# are build output, regenerated automatically on first run.
*.db

# Root package.json is unused scaffolding (no source code depends on it) —
# left ignored by default, but Assets/node_modules is explicitly un-ignored
# below per request even though nothing in the site loads from it.
node_modules/
!Assets/node_modules/
!Assets/node_modules/**

# Raw downloaded asset archives and Apple AR-only formats. Confirmed with
# `grep -r` that no .html or .js in this repo ever loads a .zip or .usdz
# file — the site only ever fetches specific named .glb files.
*.zip
*.usdz

# Unreferenced duplicate/unused 3D models left over from the same asset
# download batch. world.html's modelDefinitions list only loads
# anime_nature_tree_01.glb, buildings.glb, city.glb,
# generic_factory_with_smoke_towers.glb, low_poly_business_buildings_pack.glb,
# and low_poly_house_5.glb — these are not among them.
Portfoilos/3D & Graphics Desginer/Assets/Outside/anime_nature_tree_01 (1).glb
Portfoilos/3D & Graphics Desginer/Assets/Outside/generic_factory_with_smoke_towers (1).glb
Portfoilos/3D & Graphics Desginer/Assets/Outside/patch_of_grass.glb
Portfoilos/3D & Graphics Desginer/Assets/Outside/stylized_nature_pack_vol-1__3d_tree.glb

# 114MB — exceeds GitHub's 100MB hard per-file limit, so a normal push
# rejects it outright. Kept locally; not pushed. See the push summary for
# how to add it back via Git LFS if you want it live on GitHub.
Portfoilos/GIS & Remote Sensing/Task#1/Task#1.pdf
